    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **Lawrence Butler**, who commands our highest score of 74.61. The matchup against Ure\u00f1a is ideal, providing the perfect storm of a favorable park environment and a targetable pitcher, allowing him to capitalize on his elite sprint speed to bolster our scarcest category, SB. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** (66.12) and **Bryson Stott** (63.92) offer strong profiles. **Daulton Varsho** benefits significantly from the matchup against Rea, while **Bryson Stott** draws a tactical edge from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which historically invites higher stolen base success, making him a primary driver for our efficiency goals today.\n\n**Geraldo Perdomo** (60.32) rounds out our top-tier starts, maintaining high value despite a league-average matchup against Bradley. The decision to bench others was largely dictated by the unfavorable conditions facing the bottom of the order; specifically, **Drew Gilbert** (40.95) hovered near the threshold but was pushed down by the combination of an 8-hole assignment and an uninspiring look at Meyer. While players like **Masyn Winn**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Brendan Donovan** remain in our reserve pool, their current projections fail to eclipse the efficiency gains we expect from **Yainer Diaz** (58.35) and **Jonathan Aranda** (55.67). We continue to navigate the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Will Smith**, and **Dylan Beavers** due to injury, keeping a close watch on **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, and **Gavin Sheets** to see if any late lineup shifts warrant a rotation change to stabilize our SB output. \n\nA cautionary note on **Taylor Ward** (43.74): facing a pitcher of Yamamoto\u2019s caliber suppresses his score despite the lead-off spot. He remains a volatile play today, and we must monitor his early at-bats closely to ensure he isn't neutralized by the high-skill arm. **Cal Raleigh** (54.60) and **Matt Chapman** (52.10) are likewise high-variance options, as their scores are hampered by the defensive prowess of the opposition. We will rely on our core of **Lawrence Butler** and **Daulton Varsho** to shoulder the heavy lifting while managing these marginal starts to protect our cumulative game caps.",
